course: dictionary
lesson: 8662
title: Names and short forms
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A name tells us who someone is, and it always starts with a capital letter. Seb is a name, so you will not find it as an ordinary word you use in everyday writing.
explain: Seb is a short form of Sebastian. People shorten names to make them quicker to say, so Seb and Sebastian can be the same boy. Look at the context: «when his mate Seb asks where he's going, Kwesi mumbles «dunno yet»». Seb is a person who asks Kwesi a question, and he is Kwesi's mate, which means friend.
fact: A name is the word people use to call someone, and it begins with a capital letter.
fact: «Seb» is a short form of the boy's name Sebastian.
fact: Short forms of names are common: Sam can be short for Samuel, and Liz can be short for Elizabeth.
fact: «SEB» in capital letters can be an abbreviation used by some organisations, but this is rare.
fact: In «Seb asks where he's going», Seb is a person, not a place or an object.
exercise: In «when his mate Seb asks where he's going», who is Seb? | *A friend of Kwesi | A place Kwesi wants to visit | A school subject | A type of food
exercise: What is «Seb» a short form of? | *Sebastian | Sebastopol | Seaside | Sewing
exercise: Why does «Seb» start with a capital letter? | Because it is a long word | *Because it is a name | Because it is the first word of every sentence | Because it is a number
test: Seb is a short form of which name? | Sophie | *Sebastian | Samuel | Sebago
test: What must a name like Seb always begin with? | *A capital letter | A full stop | A question mark | A number
exam: Which word is a short form of a boy's name? | Seed | Sea | *Seb | Sew
